  "source_url": "https://www.grafs.com/catalog/product/productId/21",
  "notes": "Item 83171 (Varmint Express line on Hornady's site and in the 2022 chart, not Critical Defense). BC: third-party, independent sources agree on .115: Graf & Sons (https://www.grafs.com/catalog/product/productId/21, '.115 (G1)', ITEM # 83171); Delta Mike NZ (https://www.deltamike.co.nz/?p=55244, '.115 (G1)', item 83171); also MCARBO 17 HMR ballistics chart (https://www.mcarbo.com/17-hmr-ballistics-chart.aspx, Hornady 15.5 gr, BC .115, 2525 fps) and AmmoSight (https://ammosight.com/rimfire-ammo/17-hmr, BC .115, 2525 fps). Drag model G1 stated by Graf's and Delta Mike. No Hornady document with a BC was found (2022 Standard Ballistics Chart has no BC column). Muzzle velocity 2525 fps and 24 in test barrel from the current Hornady product page (https://www.hornady.com/ammunition/rimfire/17-hmr-15.5-gr.-ntx) and the 2022 chart. Construction: polymer-tipped NTX with a non-lead core (Hornady: 'non-traditional core material' for areas with restrictions on traditional bullets); set as polymer_tip because it is not described as monolithic. lead_free=true based on that description and retailer 'lead-free' labelling.",
  "verified_on": "2026-10-19"
 },
 {
