  "construction": "polymer_tip",
  "lead_free": false,
  "min_expansion_mps": null,
  "source_url": "https://www.grafs.com/catalog/product/productId/7019",
  "notes": "Item 83170. BC: third-party, three independent sources agree on .125 for this exact Hornady product: Graf & Sons (https://www.grafs.com/catalog/product/productId/7019, 'Ballistic Coefficient .125 (G1)', ITEM # 83170); Delta Mike NZ (https://www.deltamike.co.nz/product/hornady-17-hmr-17-gr-v-max-varmint-express-rimfire-50-rounds/, '.125 (G1)', item 83170); Shooting Times, Rick Jamison, 2011-01-04 (https://www.shootingtimes.com/editorial/ammunition_17_hmr_0508/100429): 'Hornady reports 2550 fps from a little 17-grain V-Max ... with a ballistic coefficient (B.C.) of .125' (author refers to it as Hornady's B.C. label). Also hunting-sport.com (EU, item 831701) lists 0.125 without drag model. Drag model G1 stated by Graf's and Delta Mike. No Hornady document with a BC was found: Hornady's 2022 Standard Ballistics Chart PDF lists this load but has no BC column; web.archive.org could not be fetched. Muzzle velocity 2550 fps and 24 in test barrel from the current Hornady product page (https://www.hornady.com/ammunition/rimfire/17-hmr-17-gr-v-max) and the 2022 Standard Ballistics Chart. Retailer copy gives sectional density .155, which does not match a 17 gr .172 bullet (about .082); ignored.",
  "verified_on": "2026-10-19"
 },
