  "source_url": "https://www.grafs.com/catalog/product/productId/7020",
  "notes": "Item 83172 (20 gr HP XTP). BC: third-party, independent sources agree on .125: Graf & Sons (https://www.grafs.com/catalog/product/productId/7020, 0.125 G1, ITEM # 83172); Delta Mike NZ (https://www.deltamike.co.nz/product/17-hmr-20-gr-hp-xtp-varmint-express-rimfire-50-rounds/, '.125 (G1)', item 83172, 24 in test barrel); also MCARBO 17 HMR ballistics chart (https://www.mcarbo.com/17-hmr-ballistics-chart.aspx, Hornady 20 gr, BC .125, 2375 fps). Drag model G1 stated by Graf's and Delta Mike. A search snippet attributed .225 to Kinsey's, but Kinsey's robots.txt disallows all agents so it was not read; .225 is far outside the plausible range and contradicted by the three sources above. No Hornady document with a BC was found (2022 Standard Ballistics Chart has no BC column). Muzzle velocity 2375 fps and 24 in test barrel from the current Hornady product page (https://www.hornady.com/ammunition/rimfire/17-hmr-20-gr-xtp) and the 2022 chart. Construction: jacketed hollow point (XTP), mapped to cup_and_core. Retailer copy gives sectional density .183, which does not match a 20 gr .172 bullet (about .097); ignored.",
  "verified_on": "2026-10-19"
 },
